course: dictionary
lesson: 9355
title: One word, two jobs: splinter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A splinter can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a splinter is a small, sharp, thin piece of wood, glass or metal that has broken off, often one that gets stuck in your skin. As a verb, to splinter means to break into small sharp pieces.
explain: Context tells you which job the word is doing. «Ask an adult to take out a splinter with clean tweezers» names a thing, so splinter is a noun. «Wear shoes on old wooden decks, because the wood can splinter» describes an action, so splinter is a verb.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «A splinter should be removed by a grown-up with clean tweezers, because dirty splinters get infected» tells you what to do and why. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Splinter is a noun (a splinter, splinters) and a verb (to splinter, splintered, splintering).
fact: As a noun, «splinter» means a small, sharp, thin piece of wood, glass or metal that has broken off.
fact: As a verb, «splinter» means to break into small sharp pieces.
fact: Useful phrases: get a splinter, take out a splinter, splinter group.
fact: If a splinter is stuck in your skin, wash the skin and let a grown-up take it out with clean tweezers.
exercise: «Ask an adult to take out a splinter with clean tweezers, because a splinter left in can get infected.» What is a splinter? | A tiny bug that bites | A type of plaster for cuts | A big stone on a path | *A small, sharp, thin piece of wood, glass or metal
exercise: «Wear shoes on old wooden decks, because the wood can splinter.» What does splinter mean here? | *To break into small sharp pieces | To paint something bright | To grow taller | To make a loud song
exercise: «A splinter should be removed by a grown-up with clean tweezers.» Find and copy the word that names the tool used to take out a splinter. | grown-up | *tweezers | removed | clean
test: Which phrase from the lessons means taking a splinter out of your skin? | *Take out a splinter | Old wooden decks | Break into pieces | Splinter group
test: Ryan says, «The stick began to splinter when he sat on it.» What is happening to the stick? | *It is breaking into small sharp pieces | It is being painted | It is getting warmer | It is growing new leaves
exam: What should you do if a splinter is stuck in your skin? | Push it in deeper with a pin | Pull it out with your teeth | Cover it and forget it | *Wash the skin and let a grown-up take it out with clean tweezers
